  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ACCESS TO AFFORDABLE RENEWABLE ENERGY IN LESOTHO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Renewable Lesotho: Access to Affordable and Renewable Energy project in Lesotho, implemented by UNDP, aims to increase renewable energy generation capacity and energy efficiency, promote a more equitable and gender-transformative access to clean energy, and improve Lesotho&#x2019;s energy sector leadership and institutional capacity. The objective of the grant is for Public service, commercial and industrial facilities to be equipped with renewable energy and energy efficiency solutions and improved access to clean cooking and electricity including, minigrid electricity, improved cook-stoves, solar water heaters, energy efficient lamps, PAYGO SHS, etc.) In a gender-responsive and socially inclusive manner. The project is jointly supported by UNDP and the EU, and implemented by UNDP and the government of Lesotho.</narrative>
  </description>
